~ curious
{{Global.player_name}}: That explosion. Was that your ship or something? Did you arrive here on it?
Girl: The flames. Yes, my ship, it exploded.
Narrator: She points to the distant glow, then touches her side. She's definitely hurt.
{{Global.player_name}}: I wish I could understand you. But I saw the crash. That looked... brutal.
Narrator: Her antennae move slightly, and there's something in her eyes. Relief, maybe? Or gratitude?
{{Global.player_name}}: You came all this way just to crash here. That must've been terrifying.
{{Global.player_name}}: You're running from something, aren't you?
Girl: I sense you understand, even without words.
Narrator: "pɛθov"...? That word sounded heavy coming from her, I think that might be something important.
=> curious_options

~ curious_options
- Why did you come to Earth? [if not local.curious_asked_why_earth]
	set local.curious_asked_why_earth = true

	{{Global.player_name}}: Earth, though... why here? We're not exactly advanced or anything special.
	Girl: I sense your confusion.
	Narrator: She's responding to how I feel, not what I said. Those antennae are reading me somehow.
	{{Global.player_name}}: Whatever brought you here, it must've been important. Worth risking everything for.
	Narrator: There's real pain in her eyes now. She seems to be remembering something...
